WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.170
Conan, you're coming to Los Angeles,

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:06.160
and they're building your
studio in Universal City.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.300
A bleak pit of despair,

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.029
that will crush your soul daily.

00:00:10.029 --> 00:00:10.862
(audience laughter)

00:00:10.862 --> 00:00:12.890
And, to get away from that and rejuvenate,

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:15.220
you're gonna wanna come here,

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.030
to sunny Burbank, California.

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:20.613
(upbeat music)

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:23.810
Conan, you're such a history buff,

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:24.790
we all know that,

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.000
and to scratch that itch,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.510
you're gonna wanna come here,

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:29.240
to the Burbank Historical Society.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.690
I'm in front of the Mentzer House,

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:32.400
this was built in 1887,

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.150
a year before the Jack The Ripper murders,

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.761
five years before the Beatles first L.P.

00:00:35.761 --> 00:00:36.594
(audience laughter)

00:00:36.594 --> 00:00:40.340
So, let's go inside and
let's learn about Burbank.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.820
So, I'm talking to Mary Jane Strickland,

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.580
who is the founder of the

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.718
Burbank Historical Society.

00:00:45.718 --> 00:00:47.620
You know Burbank inside and out,

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.820
so what I'm wondering is,

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.580
you know, Conan O'Brien has
a very distinctive look,

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:55.120
I mean, some would say compelling,

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.840
some would say freakish,
(audience laughter)

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.230
he has very, very distinct hair,

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:02.460
and I'm just wondering will
the residents of Burbank

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.500
kind of embrace that?

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:04.970
Like, have they seen
anything like that before?

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:05.960
Would they be okay with him?

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.150
What do you think?

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.760
Yeah, we have a lot of people with

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.420
funny hairdos in Burbank,
(audience laughter)

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.608
and we think he's very handsome.

00:01:12.608 --> 00:01:13.630
Oh, nice.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:14.463
Yes.

00:01:14.463 --> 00:01:15.330
So, people in Burbank find Conan,

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:16.310
that's good to know.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:17.240
Yes.
(audience laughter)

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:18.640
Nice.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.780
Conan, I'm standing next to a Holy relic.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.793
This is the jacket of Johnny Carson.

00:01:25.930 --> 00:01:29.343
Some day, if you shrink eight inches,

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.270
and gain some talent,
(audience laughter)

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:37.120
this will adorn your torso.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.570
Oh, it burns.
(audience laughter)

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:40.580
It burns.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:45.300
Hi, I'm in a recreation
of a 1900's Burbank home.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.430
I am here in my parlor,
(audience laughter)

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:49.690
with my wife, Opal,

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:52.670
who has gone insane.
(audience laughter)

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:53.503
Opal?

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:57.590
Opal, I know you can hear me.
(audience laughter)

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:00.411
We're gonna take you to the
nervous hospital now, Opal.

00:02:00.411 --> 00:02:01.244
(audience laughter)

00:02:01.244 --> 00:02:04.650
You'll stop seeing those laughing ghosts,

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:06.850
that force you to draw pictures

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:08.580
of swords that look like penises.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.416
Opal!
(audience laughter)

00:02:11.416 --> 00:02:12.295
Opal!

00:02:12.295 --> 00:02:13.399
(disembodied scream)

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:14.610
(scary music)

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.250
By the way, I just wanted
you guys to see this.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.700
When you shoot stuff in L.A.,

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:18.730
even if it's something stupid,

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:19.980
like what we're doing right now,

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.480
they assign you a cop.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.230
A cop has to be there for security,

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:24.930
look who they gave me.

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.700
They gave me a friggen superhero.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:27.650
Look at this guy!
(audience laughter)

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:28.928
What's your first name?

00:02:28.928 --> 00:02:29.761
Gammer.

00:02:29.761 --> 00:02:30.594
Gammer?
Yes, sir.

00:02:30.594 --> 00:02:31.580
More like, you know what?

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:32.820
Gammer-Man,

00:02:32.820 --> 00:02:34.240
that's who they assigned to me,

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:35.450
Gammer-Man.

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.383
He's made of pure quartz and tornadoes.

00:02:38.383 --> 00:02:39.216
(audience laughter)

00:02:39.216 --> 00:02:41.400
He's made of five tornadoes,

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.690
Good God in Heaven.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:43.523
My pleasure, sir.

00:02:43.523 --> 00:02:45.318
No, hey, my pleasure.
(audience laughter)

00:02:45.318 --> 00:02:46.890
(quirky music)

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.790
And, there's so many great
business names here in Burbank,

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.320
like, Hollywoof Dog Grooming,

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.190
Hair To Please,

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:56.810
Victorian Hairitage.

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.350
And, don't forget the business names that

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.720
sound great when said by Jerry Lewis,

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.820
like, Delsen Building,

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.170
Boysen Plaza,
(audience laughter)

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:08.570
Chadaka Thai,
(audience laughter)

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:10.226
and Old Navy!

00:03:10.226 --> 00:03:11.970
(audience laughter)

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:12.803
This is Kerry Hite,

00:03:12.803 --> 00:03:15.310
she's the owner of the
Wax Poetic Beauty Salon

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.560
right here in Burbank,

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.171
where I come to get my hair done.

00:03:18.171 --> 00:03:19.810
Uhhh, uhhh, uhhh.
(audience laughter)

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:22.120
Wax Poetic, Conan, is where you can come

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:24.120
and not only get your hair done,

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:24.953
you can read a book.

00:03:24.953 --> 00:03:26.660
Uh oh, Britney.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:27.770
You can look at art.

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:29.390
Admire.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:30.230
But, you know what?

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:32.400
Why should I talk about
it when I can show you

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.110
what a day at Wax Poetic Salon looks like.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.390
Lets go check it out.

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:37.329
(relaxing music)

00:03:37.329 --> 00:03:38.760
Hmm.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.301
(screams)

00:03:40.301 --> 00:03:42.031
(moaning)

00:03:42.031 --> 00:03:43.458
(screams)

00:03:43.458 --> 00:03:44.595
(screams expletive)

00:03:44.595 --> 00:03:45.428
(audience laughter)

00:03:45.428 --> 00:03:47.520
Do you like paintings by serial killers?

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.020
Then come next door to Hyaena.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:53.360
And nothing says John Wayne Gacy

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:55.253
like a clown in a graveyard,

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:57.230
and at Hyaena,

00:03:57.230 --> 00:03:59.700
you can get all kinds of decorations for

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.280
Christmas.
(audience laughter)

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:02.370
Easter.
(audience laughter)

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:03.640
First Communion.
(audience laughter)

00:04:03.640 --> 00:04:05.480
Hanukkah.
(audience laughter)

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:06.330
Oh my goodness,

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.690
I just finished another
delicious lunch here,

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:09.890
at the Olives Bistro,

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.470
inside The Coast Hotel,

00:04:11.470 --> 00:04:13.660
but what made this lunch pretty amazing

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:16.450
was that I was served by
the restaurant's manager,

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.160
Rob Lambaren,

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:19.733
better known as,

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:24.070
Rawbzilla, competitive breakdancer.

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.380
You're a competitive break dancer?

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.110
Yeah.
And, you're world class?

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:27.943
Yes.

00:04:27.943 --> 00:04:30.030
You go up against Germans, Czechs,

00:04:30.030 --> 00:04:31.940
Chinese, and Russians?

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:32.773
Everything, yeah.

00:04:32.773 --> 00:04:33.630
You take 'em all on?

00:04:33.630 --> 00:04:34.610
Mm-hmm.
17 years?

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:35.443
17 years, yeah.

00:04:35.443 --> 00:04:38.880
17 years, and so you manage
the restaurant to pay for

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:39.923
the break dancing?

00:04:39.923 --> 00:04:40.756
Yeah.

00:04:40.756 --> 00:04:41.589
That is dedication.

00:04:41.589 --> 00:04:42.460
If you don't mind,

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:44.140
I'm going to finish my coffee,

00:04:44.140 --> 00:04:45.520
and you're gonna bust some moves.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.280
It helps with my digestion.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.460
Yes, sir.

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:50.960
(funky music)

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.640
Glorious.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:04.410
Well, it's been an amazing
day here in Burbank,

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:06.150
I'll bet you can't wait to get here.

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:07.280
It's time for me to scoot.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.887
Gammer, let's go home.

00:05:08.887 --> 00:05:13.054
(audience laughter and applause)

